WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.480 --> 00:00:17.126
One day Robin was talking to Will Scarlet.

2
00:00:17.146 --> 00:00:19.007
"We're running low on money.

3
00:00:19.587 --> 00:00:20.728
How will we help the poor?"

4
00:00:21.608 --> 00:00:22.429
"What about a feast?"

5
00:00:22.889 --> 00:00:23.409
asked Will.

6
00:00:23.429 --> 00:00:26.971
"Yes!" said Robin.

7
00:00:26.991 --> 00:00:29.792
"Go find a rich man and bring him to eat with us."

8
00:00:32.648 --> 00:00:35.431
Will and several men went to the road and waited.

9
00:00:36.211 --> 00:00:39.434
Many people passed by, but there were no rich people.

10
00:00:41.215 --> 00:00:45.799
The men ate some lunch and took a nap, and at last the sun began to set.

11
00:00:45.819 --> 00:00:49.763
"Let's go home," said Will.

12
00:00:50.864 --> 00:00:54.247
The men had just started walking when Will stopped abruptly.

13
00:00:54.267 --> 00:00:56.388
"Shh. I hear something!"

14
00:00:57.489 --> 00:00:59.971
The others listened and soon they heard it too.

15
00:01:00.744 --> 00:01:03.505
A young man sat by a stream, crying!

16
00:01:05.465 --> 00:01:09.006
His blond hair was messy and his clothes looked rumpled.

17
00:01:10.027 --> 00:01:13.307
Over his head a wooden harp hung from a tree branch.

18
00:01:13.327 --> 00:01:16.968
"You're Alan of Dale, the minstrel," said Will.

19
00:01:16.988 --> 00:01:21.070
"Yes." Alan reached for his harp with a sigh.

20
00:01:21.090 --> 00:01:23.730
"What's wrong?"

21
00:01:24.130 --> 00:01:24.671
asked Will.

22
00:01:24.691 --> 00:01:30.188
"I want to marry a beautiful girl named Ellen.

23
00:01:30.208 --> 00:01:32.609
Her father doesn't like me because I'm poor.

24
00:01:33.349 --> 00:01:39.451
This morning I learned some terrible news—she's marrying Sir Stephen of Trent.

25
00:01:40.751 --> 00:01:43.372
He's an old man, but he's rich.

26
00:01:44.172 --> 00:01:46.252
And the wedding's in two days!"

27
00:01:46.272 --> 00:01:48.833
"Come home with us," said Will.

28
00:01:48.853 --> 00:01:51.614
"I'm sure Robin Hood can find a way to help you."

29
00:01:53.474 --> 00:01:56.955
They walked through the forest and soon arrived at the big oak tree.

30
00:01:56.975 --> 00:02:00.841
"You didn't bring me a rich man," said Robin.

31
00:02:00.861 --> 00:02:02.842
"No," said Will.

32
00:02:02.862 --> 00:02:06.065
"This is Alan of Dale, and he has a problem."

33
00:02:06.865 --> 00:02:09.628
Robin listened carefully to Alan's story.

34
00:02:10.388 --> 00:02:13.391
The young man was obviously full of sorrow.

35
00:02:13.411 --> 00:02:16.413
"I think I have a plan," said Robin.

36
00:02:16.433 --> 00:02:21.097
"But tell me something first—are you sure Ellen wants to marry you?"

37
00:02:21.117 --> 00:02:22.918
"Oh, yes!"

38
00:02:23.299 --> 00:02:24.079
Alan replied.

39
00:02:24.099 --> 00:02:25.740
"We're engaged."

40
00:02:25.760 --> 00:02:28.803
"Then the solution is simple," said Robin.

41
00:02:28.823 --> 00:02:31.469
"All we need is a friar to marry you."

42
00:02:31.489 --> 00:02:34.412
"I know the friar of Fountain Abbey," said Will.

43
00:02:34.432 --> 00:02:36.494
"Robin, I'll guide you to the abbey."

44
00:02:37.115 --> 00:02:38.956
"I'll go tomorrow morning," Robin said.

45
00:02:38.976 --> 00:02:40.858
"And don't worry, Alan.

46
00:02:41.839 --> 00:02:44.361
You'll soon be married to the lovely Ellen!"

47
00:02:47.284 --> 00:02:49.686
The next day Will led Robin to a river.

48
00:02:49.706 --> 00:02:51.168
"I'll leave you here.

49
00:02:51.869 --> 00:02:53.050
The abbey is easy to find.

50
00:02:53.710 --> 00:02:55.352
You can cross the river just around the bend."

51
00:02:56.532 --> 00:03:01.035
Robin walked along the river and soon spotted a stout man—a friar.

52
00:03:01.935 --> 00:03:04.056
He had curly black hair and red cheeks.

53
00:03:04.717 --> 00:03:06.958
His gray eyes danced with humor.

54
00:03:06.978 --> 00:03:09.899
"Hello!" called Robin.

55
00:03:09.919 --> 00:03:12.501
"Do you know the friar of Fountain Abbey?"

56
00:03:13.201 --> 00:03:15.923
"Yes, somewhat," answered the friar.

57
00:03:15.943 --> 00:03:20.485
"I believe I must cross the river to find him," Robin went on.

58
00:03:20.505 --> 00:03:23.227
"But I don't want to get my nice clothes wet.

59
00:03:24.287 --> 00:03:25.328
You look very strong.

60
00:03:25.944 --> 00:03:27.084
Will you carry me across?"

61
00:03:27.104 --> 00:03:30.225
"What?" cried the friar.

62
00:03:30.965 --> 00:03:35.327
Then he remembered he was a religious man and should do good deeds.

63
00:03:35.347 --> 00:03:38.027
"Fine. I'll do it," he said.

64
00:03:38.047 --> 00:03:41.928
"Let me carry your sword so it stays dry."

65
00:03:43.109 --> 00:03:46.830
Robin gave the friar his sword and climbed onto the man's back.

66
00:03:47.610 --> 00:03:48.590
They crossed the river.

67
00:03:50.931 --> 00:03:54.432
On the other side, the friar looked slyly at Robin.

68
00:03:55.472 --> 00:03:57.874
"I want to return to the other side.

69
00:03:58.235 --> 00:04:00.076
But I'm too wet and tired.

70
00:04:00.897 --> 00:04:04.840
Now it's your turn—you must carry me back across."

71
00:04:04.860 --> 00:04:09.044
"What?" This time Robin was outraged.

72
00:04:09.844 --> 00:04:12.827
But the friar refused to return Robin's sword.

73
00:04:13.667 --> 00:04:18.712
So Robin had no choice but to pick up the friar and carry him across the river.

74
00:04:18.732 --> 00:04:21.214
"Where's my sword?"

75
00:04:21.754 --> 00:04:22.495
asked the friar.

76
00:04:22.515 --> 00:04:23.836
"Right here!"

77
00:04:24.488 --> 00:04:28.990
Robin had managed to seize the friar's sword as well as his own sword.

78
00:04:29.010 --> 00:04:30.651
"I'll give it to you.

79
00:04:31.411 --> 00:04:33.592
But you must carry me across the river again."

80
00:04:33.612 --> 00:04:37.053
"Fine," grumbled the friar.

81
00:04:37.894 --> 00:04:38.974
He picked up Robin.

82
00:04:40.315 --> 00:04:43.716
Halfway across the river, the friar stopped for a moment.

83
00:04:44.296 --> 00:04:49.078
Then, with a sudden lift of his hand, he dumped Robin into the water.

84
00:04:51.599 --> 00:04:57.386
Robin leaped up and the men began to fight on land with swords.

85
00:04:59.987 --> 00:05:02.188
The two men fought for a long time.

86
00:05:02.889 --> 00:05:06.111
At last Robin blew his horn three times.

87
00:05:06.991 --> 00:05:09.612
Will Scarlet appeared with a large group of men.

88
00:05:10.393 --> 00:05:16.296
But the friar whistled loudly and suddenly four fierce dogs ran at Robin!

89
00:05:16.316 --> 00:05:18.838
They chased him up a tree.

90
00:05:18.858 --> 00:05:23.000
"Help!" cried Robin.

91
00:05:24.936 --> 00:05:27.458
Will stepped forward to call the dogs.

92
00:05:28.198 --> 00:05:31.160
They instantly ran to him and licked his face.

93
00:05:31.180 --> 00:05:34.762
"Will?" cried the friar in surprise.

94
00:05:34.782 --> 00:05:36.663
"Is that you?

95
00:05:37.343 --> 00:05:38.724
What are you doing here?"

96
00:05:38.744 --> 00:05:41.826
"I brought Robin Hood to meet you," said Will.

97
00:05:45.588 --> 00:05:47.169
Robin climbed down the tree.

98
00:05:47.189 --> 00:05:49.090
"Robin," said Will.

99
00:05:49.110 --> 00:05:52.472
"This is Friar Tuck, the friar of Fountain Abbey!"

100
00:05:53.088 --> 00:05:55.351
The two men laughed and shook hands.

101
00:05:55.371 --> 00:05:58.554
"I need your help, Friar," Robin said.

102
00:05:58.574 --> 00:06:00.236
"Please come home with us."
